e `if cc != 0: return cc`). Then:\n\n```\n  260 +         log_row(job, \"closed\", ...)   ← 8-space indent?\n```\n\nThe listing shows `  260 +         log_row(...` — 8 spaces + content, i.e., same indent as `if doc.get(\"terminal_state\") in TERMINALS:` (line 243, context, 8 spaces). And line 263 `if doc.get(\"terminal_state\") not in TERMINALS:` also 8 spaces, with line 264 print at 12.\n\nSo structure:\n\n```python\n        if doc.get(\"terminal_state\") in TERMINALS:      # 8\n            print(\"\\ncustody:\")                          # 12\n            cargs = [...]                                # 12\n            ...\n            cc = call(...)                               # 12\n            if cc != 0:                                  # 12\n                ...return cc                             # 16\n            vc, kind = run_verifier(job, a)              # 12? \n```\n\nHmm wait, line 255 in the listing: `  255 +             vc, kind = run_verifier(job, a)` — let me count: the listing format is `NNNN + ` then code. Line 248: `  248 +             cc = call(\"emit_custody.py\", cargs)` — that's 12 spaces. Line 255: `  255 +             vc, kind = run_verifier(job, a)` — 12 spaces. Lines 256-259: 12/16 spaces. Line 260: `  260 +         log_row(job, \"closed\", ...` — 8 spaces. Line 263: `  263 +         if doc.get(\"terminal_state\") not in TERMINALS:` — 8 spaces.\n\nAnd line 243 (context): `  243           if doc.get(\"terminal_state\") in TERMINALS:` — hmm, how many spaces? The listing line is `  243           if doc...` — after \"243\" there are spaces then \"if\". Context lines show \"NNNN \" + code with original indentation preserved. Comparing: line 244 `  244               print(\"\\ncustody:\")` — 12 spaces after the marker? Let me align: `  244 ` then `            print(...)` — 12 spaces. And 243: `  243           if doc.get(...)` — hmm, 243 shows `          if doc...` — that's 10 characters between \"243 \" and \"if\"? Hard to count exactly from the