lies to the allowance's writer, and shadow-checks recompute hand sets from the same ledger — consistent trust model. OK.\n\nAlso: `check_events` compares record arrays to ledger verbatim; a forged ledger line rides into the record and the verifier recomputes from the same ledger — shadow passes. But that's the trust model (ledger is live-stamped evidence; same as base). Fine.\n\nVerdict: CONFORMS.\n\nActually — hold on, one more scan of point 1 for the `emit_custody.py` docstring line 66 removal → 67-74: the exit-3 description now lists hand-time refusal etc. And \"A routing request that did not ask OpenRouter for the pin alone with no fallback and ZDR is a hard gap (exit 1), not a refusal\" — retained from old (present in both old 66 and new 72-73). ✓\n\nAnd `Gaps`/`hard` unchanged. `rel_file` unchanged. `maker_history` no-log refusal retained. `evaluator_history` retained. `link_call` retained (context). `annotate` retained. Good.\n\nAlso `custody_history.py` line 219: `read_log(path, ref=None, who=\"log\")` — the emitter still passes its real ref everywhere it did before (maker_history: `H.read_log(log, ref, \"maker\")` — yes line 1001). ✓\n\nFinal answer: CONFORMS.\n\nLINES: kit/emit_custody.py:881, kit/emit_custody.py:1020, kit/emit_custody.py:1203, kit/plumbline_job.py:256, kit/plumbline_job.py:259, kit/plumbline_job.py:99, kit/plumbline_verify.py:393, kit/plumbline_verify.py:919\n\nREASON: The switch reaches only the block that adds `hand-time` refusals — every other refusal, cross-check and check_order runs unconditionally whether or not it is set (e.g. the startedAt/producedAt cross-checks at emit_custody.py:1020-1021 still fire for allowed hand times) — and the close runs plumbline_verify after emitting and refuses (close_refused row, no `closed` row, verifier's exit code) on any failure including cannot-run when no checker is configured, so it cannot be bypassed; the verifier itself fails unflagged hand times and runs the schema/required-field layer first