e 12-record call above was retried five times before anyone resized it... the right reading is 'resize', not 'retry'.\" Explicitly draws the correct lesson. Not a contradiction.\n\nOne more: line 44 story: \"an instrument was frozen with an 800-token cap. All three scoring calls spent about 798 tokens reasoning and returned empty. The batch was void, and the Owner had to approve an amendment to rerun it.\" Past failure. Fine.\n\nLine 51: \"The doctrine-pointer job did it right: both pinned providers were live-tested before freeze.\" Fine.\n\nHmm, one more potential: line 96 \"Give the Maker... clock cutoff\" — fine.\n\nLine 100 story: the best-artifact check passed but request didn't contain the guide; fix was pinned step. Fine.\n\nLine 102: \"attempt 2, with byte-identical messages, after the Owner's own yes in the Maker's chat.\" Wait — \"after the Owner's own yes in the Maker's chat\" — the Owner approved in the Maker's chat; the Orchestrator didn't witness it. Line 17 says relayed approvals are not approvals and only Owner's own words approve. Here it says \"the Owner's own yes in the Maker's chat\" — that's the Owner's own words, in the Maker's chat channel. B8 says only the Owner's own words approve — this was the Owner's own yes. So fine. And line 107-108: \"Ask the Maker to quote the Owner's go-ahead in its report. You need it for the close line, and you did not see it happen.\" Fine.\n\nHmm, but B8 also says \"A relayed approval is a report, not an approval\" — the go-ahead in the Maker's chat is the Owner speaking directly in that chat, not a relay. Fine.\n\nLine 129: \"Even in a void batch, look for real signal\" — fine.\n\nOK — one more careful look at potential contradiction with doctrine §5 exits: \"Below the cap, such work goes back to the Maker. The best version the job produced goes to the Owner, never to the bin.\" Guide line 136: at cap → needs owner. Fine.\n\nDoctrine §5: \"There is no state in which a loop quietly ends.\" Guide: every path ends 